This warning is a false positive.
At [tiny_ef.rs (line 26)](/home/ubuntu/Projects/experimental/analyzer/UnSAT-Rust/benchmark/ruklee/ptr_hash-0.1.1/src/tiny_ef.rs:26):
for i in (0..vals.len()).step_by(L) {
    // L = 44
    min(i + L, vals.len())
}
The relevant invariants are:
- i < vals.len().
- A valid Rust &[u64] cannot have a byte size greater than isize::MAX.
- Consequently, vals.len() <= isize::MAX / size_of::<u64>(), far below usize::MAX.
- Therefore i + 44 cannot overflow usize.
MIRAI tracks i as an insufficiently bounded usize and misses the maximum-size invariant of a valid slice.
Verdict: FP — 0 TP, 1 FP.
Note that min(i + L, vals.len()) alone would not prevent overflow because addition occurs before min; safety comes from the slice-length bound. Using i.saturating_add(L).min(vals.len()) could silence analyzers, though it is not required for correctness here.

